      'The graduate answer-key listing (aerolink_grad_key_assume_require.sysml) lives in sysml/instructor/week10: it is validated with the other listings, excluded from the app bundle (src/lib/sysml.ts, tested) and referenced from no student block. A student with access to the repository could still read it; keep the repository private to staff if that matters.',
      'Workload (AUTHORING_GUIDE §7 rule 3; WORKLOAD_ANALYSIS.md): budget 9.5 h. Readings are 21 slides at ≈ 30 sl/h (0.7 h) plus the three S06 pages the lesson cites, p.161, 165 and 168 (0.2 h at ≈ 15 pp/h). The lesson is ≈ 4,970 counted words including the probe table (trimmed from 5,095 after the sign-off review, S10-N7), at the top of the guide’s ≈ 1 h range, and the row also covers the three activities, including three translations before class: a slower reader needs ≈ 1.2–1.4 h, which puts the realistic total ≈ 0.2–0.4 h above the figures below. L10 out of class is the lab plan’s 3.5 h, which includes the CP2 requirements not finished in class (the in-class step covers the REQ-SYS set). The graduate memo is budgeted at 1 h: one new S06 page (p.162; p.161 and 165 are already read), about 0.4 h to adapt the still-air listing and run the checker, and about 0.5 h for a one-page memo answering (a)–(d); the earlier version (six pages, five parts) was realistically 1.5–2 h and was cut to fit. Realistic total ≈ 9.5 h (graduate), ≈ 8.5 h (others). Under DECISION_LOG A14 option B (graduate tasks in alternate weeks) Week 10 is a required graduate-task week; Week 9’s memo is optional. The risk is L10: teams with weak CP2/CP3 artefacts will need more than 3.5 h, which the reference model v0.2 (recovery input) mitigates; a graduate student who writes a new actor or calc def rather than adapting the listing will need ≈ 1.5 h for the memo.',
      'Open lead requests (sign-off review S10-N3; kept here because a week marked independently reviewed carries no openIssues, and listed in the notes): (1) Lead (register): add the standard-library ModelingMetadata page (StatusInfo, StatusKind, Issue; S06 §9), used by the gap convention, and the S06 section defining := (initial) and default values, mentioned uncited in q10-7. (2) Lead (reference model, W10-F07): bind REQ-SYS-010’s limit to the satisfier, attribute connectionLimit : PowerValue = chargingSystem.connectionLimit; (probe R10 PASS), and update referenceTranslations.ts and the drift tests in the same change. (3) Lead (reference model, W10-F17): the REQ-SYS-001 rationale ends “(open point for the graduate memo)”, which hints at memo part (d); drop the parenthesis or accept the hint. (4) Lead (reference model): keep REQ-SYS-007 without a still-air gate (the lesson recommends the reference-condition reading); optionally rename designTripBlockTime to stillAirBlockTime or say “still air” in its doc. (5) Lead (register, W10-F16 / S10-N5): R83 is an extension reading, but the lesson and five quiz items depend on S06 p.161–162 and 165–168; promote those pages to a Week 10 reading (they are already budgeted).',
